Hi Erica,

Sorry to hear that you're having so much trouble! On Windows, in order to facilitate isolation, we attempt to use junction points (folder shortcuts) to link external libraries into the packrat project -- for whatever reason, we are unable to create those junction points in your `lib-ext` folder. The error message, 'Access is definied', seems to suggest that the R session does not have write permissions in that folder -- and I do not know why this would be the case.

My recommendation is having your project explicitly depend on MYPACKAGE, rather than having it set as an external package (note that, either way, you will need to reinstall MYPACKAGE if you make any changes to it).

The 'story' on how packrat can be used to manage local projects is somewhat incomplete, unfortunately. As an alternative, you could try creating a 'custom CRAN repository' and placing MYPACKAGE there -- the notes at http://rstudio.github.io/packrat/custom-repos.html might be helpful, although you would need to adopt a workflow where the package is uploaded + reinstalled whenever you make changes.

This is definitely a workflow we want to accommodate (having local, under development packages work seamlessly with CRAN / other packages), so any suggestions on how you feel this process should work would be very helpful.

Thanks,
Kevin

